linux-webauthn for Debian/Ubuntu
================================

The package installs the authenticator as a systemd user service. The daemon
runs in the logged-in user's session and uses the existing Linux fingerprint
and TPM stack; it does not require a root daemon.

After installation, the user service is loaded from /usr/lib/systemd/user and
is pulled into the user's default.target. The D-Bus service and UHID udev rule
are installed as part of the same package.

To inspect the service after installation:

  systemctl --user status linux-webauthn.service
  busctl --user status org.linux.WebAuthn
